{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/798299-so-did-leeches-and-fera-get-along-in-mesoamerica","id":798299,"title":"So did Leeches and Fera Get along in Mesoamerica?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T09:49:58-08:00","id":798299,"title":"So did Leeches and Fera Get along in Mesoamerica?","content":"So, from what I've read, The local Jaguar bastet rulled openly as gods, The local Leeches (most notably the Tlacique, A Followers of Set bloodline) Ruled there too. When the europeans came the European Garou Tribes (well, primarily shadow lords, but they probably weren't alone) and Vampiric sects threw both from their high positions. But before that they both ruled openly; Did they get along, or did they hold different cities, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T10:51:46-08:00","id":798317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/798299-so-did-leeches-and-fera-get-along-in-mesoamerica#post798299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, from what I've read, The local Jaguar bastet rulled openly as gods, The local Leeches (most notably the Tlacique, A Followers of Set bloodline) Ruled there too. When the europeans came the European Garou Tribes (well, primarily shadow lords, but they probably weren't alone) and Vampiric sects threw both from their high positions. But before that they both ruled openly; Did they get along, or did they hold different cities, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering conflict between city-states for dominance was the norm afaik, at least in what today is Mexico, Guatemala &amp; Belize, i would say the latter was most probably the norm, with some cities under Balam domination, others influenced by kindred, mages, fae, wraiths, Earthbound or whatever and a bunch more in the control of wholy human rulers, with maybe some hedge magic or true faith for extra oomph.<br /> <br /> That said, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inca_Empire\" target=\"_blank\">Inca Empire</a> across the Andes was a quite different animal in that it was a relatively recent development and very strongly ordered cultural and administratively, taking much longer than the Aztec and Mayans to fold - and serve as inspiration for <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%BApac_Amaru_II\" target=\"_blank\">great insurgents</a> centuries after the fact. Anyway, just my first thoughts, hope it helps a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}